prompt:
Use case: style-transfer / precise-object-edit.
Produce a revised EVA construction exosuit sprite for a RimWorld mod, finding the middle ground between the provided two iterations.
Image 1: original concept, KEEP its mechanical structure and recognizable SCV-inspired character; user found its rendering overly polished and elaborate.
Image 2: simplified rejected version, user found it crude and empty. Do NOT use its featureless torso, U-shaped toy arm, featureless shoulder polygons, or icon-like treatment.
Image 3: actual project sprite sheet, AUTHORITATIVE reference for line weights, flat panel color, modest mechanical detail and narrow edge shading. Match the style of the energy recovery and temperature modules along the bottom row.
Return one complete isolated unit, centered on genuinely transparent square canvas. Same broad overall composition as image 1, compact yellow industrial shoulder housings, gray-white central single-person pressure cockpit, dark desaturated cyan glass, rear life-support pack, left articulated gripper and right cutter/welder arm. Face toward the bottom of the canvas, overhead game-sprite view. No feet protruding far out, no scene or text.
Make a MIDDLE-DETAIL game asset. Retain:
- shoulder housings with ONE panel seam each and a small dark inset at their rear;
- each elbow has ONE visible circular pivot and a short gray connecting forearm;
- gripper has two distinct angular jaws connected to a compact palm;
- cutting tool has two dark aperture slots and one small orange working tip;
- cockpit has one narrow gray frame, a dark glass shape, ONE restrained flat reflection patch, one small access panel on lower torso;
- backpack has one central rectangular lid and two short cylindrical side nozzle housings;
- a pair of short simple waist/boot shapes tucked closely to the torso.
Each part must have structural purpose. Use controlled fine dark contour lines, thinner interior seams. Flat subdued mustard yellow and neutral gray paint, one narrow light edge and one narrow darker edge per large panel. Keep center areas flat. Hard-edged simple shadows only. No continuous gradients, glossy specular sheen, deep sculpted facets, layered concentric borders or large black gutters. No photorealistic material, bolts, wire nests, tiny repeated vents, decals, scratches, microdetails.
Do not reduce it to a logo or geometric icon. It should look like finished RimWorld machinery with moderate functional detail, comparable to the reference modules. At 48 pixels it should have a clear cockpit, shoulder pack and two different tools; enlarged it should still have tidy mechanical joints and panel construction.
Only one sprite. No captions, no comparison sheet, no effects, no shadow, no background.
